        <title type="html"><![CDATA[New HTML setters]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46127</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46127"/>
        <updated>2026-10-13T20:52:54.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10931297?u=600cfcb4c4e709dfbc66b328147d846ee87b1e51&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>

<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>

<p dir="auto">This documents the static HTML setters as detailed here:<br>
<a href="https://developer.chrome.com/docs/web-platform/declarative-partial-updates#renewed_html_insertion_and_streaming_methods" rel="nofollow">https://developer.chrome.com/docs/web-platform/declarative-partial-updates#renewed_html_insertion_and_streaming_methods</a></p>
<p dir="auto">I have excluded the streaming APIs (will follow up with that in a future PR), and also excluded <code class="notranslate">TrustedParserOptions</code> (will follow up with that in a future PR).</p>
<p dir="auto">This is quite a big PR, but most of it is copied and pasted from the existing <code class="notranslate">setHTML()</code> and <code class="notranslate">setHMTLUnsafe()</code> docs with minor updates.</p>
<p dir="auto">There is a lot of duplication here though so I'm open to ideas of how to structure this better if we want minimal docs in <code class="notranslate">ShadowRoot</code> and <code class="notranslate">CharacterData</code> versions of these docs and leave the main docs to just the <code class="notranslate">Element</code> versions of these APIs and reference it? Or alternatively we could leave most of the docs in <code class="notranslate">setHTML</code>, <code class="notranslate">setHTMLUnsafe</code> and reference those from the other docs?</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>

<p dir="auto">These will be <a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5054329641893888" rel="nofollow">released in Chrome 157</a> (they are currently available behind a flag) and have also been merged in to the HTML Living standard (<a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5063528426" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/12753" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/whatwg/html/pull/12753/hovercard" href="https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12753">whatwg/html#12753</a>)</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>

<p dir="auto">Docs: <a href="https://developer.chrome.com/docs/web-platform/declarative-partial-updates#renewed_html_insertion_and_streaming_methods" rel="nofollow">https://developer.chrome.com/docs/web-platform/declarative-partial-updates#renewed_html_insertion_and_streaming_methods</a><br>
Chrome Status: <a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5054329641893888" rel="nofollow">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5054329641893888</a><br>
Spec PR: <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5063528426" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/12753" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/whatwg/html/pull/12753/hovercard" href="https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12753">whatwg/html#12753</a></p>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>



<p dir="auto">They were already added to BCD in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5249884576" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30328" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30328/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30328">mdn/browser-compat-data#30328</a> and will follow up with spec links when <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5745426411" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/w3c/webref/issues/2086" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/w3c/webref/pull/2086/hovercard" href="https://github.com/w3c/webref/pull/2086">w3c/webref#2086</a> is merged</p>
]]></content>
