        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Fix the broken reference to examples in Using readable byte streams]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46067</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46067"/>
        <updated>2026-10-09T00:30:26.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52491201?u=b42786e44b729e060623dfa59f38369927cdb787&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">In <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Streams_API/Using_readable_byte_streams" rel="nofollow">Using readable byte streams</a>, the note in "Underlying push source with byte reader" ends with:</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">This is similar to the behavior shown in the "pull: underlying byte source examples.</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto">The quote is never closed, and there's no section with that name on the page. This replaces it with links to the two examples that show the behavior the note describes:</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">This is similar to the behavior shown in the <a href="#underlying_pull_source_with_default_reader">Underlying pull source with default reader</a> and <a href="#underlying_pull_source_with_default_reader_and_no_allocation">Underlying pull source with default reader and no allocation</a> examples.</p>
</blockquote>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">Readers can't tell which examples the note means, and the unclosed quote reads like a typo.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<p dir="auto">The note is about using a byte source with a default reader, with and without automatic buffer allocation. Those are exactly the two examples linked: the first sets <code class="notranslate">autoAllocateChunkSize</code>, and the second doesn't, so data is enqueued. I'm inferring that these are the intended targets from the content of the note; if you had a different section in mind, I'm happy to change the links.</p>
<p dir="auto">This sentence has been there since the page was first written in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="1253462394" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/16818" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/16818/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/16818">#16818</a>, so I couldn't find an earlier version to go back to. I linked to the sections the same way the page already does elsewhere.</p>
<p dir="auto">I checked that no other open PR touches this file.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto">None.</p>]]></content>
